    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23943" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεκ-τικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>fit for receiving,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ τῆς τροφῆς δ.</span>
			<i>the part that receives</i> the food (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ κοιλία</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1290b27
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>HA</u>
				489a3
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰσθητήριον δ. τῶν αἰσθητῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>PA</u>
					647a7
				</span></i>
			; [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦ εἴδους</span>] <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Metaph.</u>
				1023a12
			</span></i>: 
				Comp.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				966a12
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>capable of,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιστήμης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Def.</u>
					415a
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐναντιώσεων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>GC</u>
					320a4
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς ἕξεως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Cat.</u>
					12a30
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διατάξεως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Porph.
					<u>Abst.</u>
					1.7
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παθημάτων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hierocl.
					<u>in CA</u>
					24p.470M.
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θυμοῦ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Ir.</u>
					p.87
				</span></i>
			 W.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόνων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Demetr.Lac.
					<u>Herc.</u>
					1012.45
				</span></i>
			 F., cf. <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>D.</u>
				1.2
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> abs.,
				<i>capable of receiving, recipient,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>de An.</u>
				414a10
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ph.</u>
				249a2
			</span></i>.</div>
